=== day
n: 4
title: JavaScript: first steps
subtitle: Values, variables, maths
hours: 3 hours
page: show.html
slot: js | js | app.js
file: app.js = js
refs: @page

--- intro
Today you write your first **JavaScript**, the language that makes a page *do* things. HTML says what things are, CSS says how they look, and JavaScript gives the browser instructions.

You work on the Friends page again. It's styled with the ShowShelf look (and your colours from Day 2), but some parts are empty: grey notes say what's missing. By the end of the day your JavaScript fills them in: the title, the facts, how long it takes to watch every episode, and a message that changes depending on the numbers.

Your code goes in a file called **app.js**. Keep an eye on the **Console** under the preview: it's where JavaScript talks back to you.

Go slowly. Every step is small on purpose, and every step saves automatically.

--- template
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
